{%- comment -%}
  Bush Riding hero — full-bleed photograph/video filling the viewport under
  the floating nav. Two chip buttons sit centred just below the nav: one
  linking to the featured product (Bush Riding Shorts), one to the map
  (BUSH MAP™ → map.bushriding.cc).
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="alp alp-hero">
  <div class="alp-hero__media">
    {%- comment -%}
      Clip first, image second. It used to be the other way round, which meant
      setting a poster image silently disabled the video — the opposite of what
      anyone filling in both fields expects. The image is now the poster.

      The src is deferred (data-alp-video, see alpine.js) rather than autoplay:
      the hero is above the fold so it starts immediately anyway, but going
      through the same path as every other clip means one place decides when
      video loads. No `type` on a source element either — a .mov declared as
      video/mp4 is rejected outright by the browser, which is exactly how the
      home page's clip went missing once already.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.video_url != blank -%}
      {%- assign hero_poster = section.settings.poster | default: section.settings.image -%}
      <video
        data-alp-video="{{ section.settings.video_url }}"
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="none"
        aria-hidden="true"
        {% if hero_poster != blank %}poster="{{ hero_poster | image_url: width: 1800 }}"{% endif %}
      ></video>
    {%- elsif section.settings.image != blank -%}
      {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 3200 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', alt: section.settings.image.alt | default: '' }}
    {%- else -%}
      <img src="{{ 'alpine-ph-hero.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="800" height="1000" loading="eager"
        data-asset-note="Full-bleed hero: hiker on mossy terrain against a pale blown-out sky, as in frame f_01">
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The veil is what makes the hero readable and what makes it olive. It runs
    0.70 → 0.92 down the frame rather than a flat fill, so the photograph still
    has somewhere to breathe at the top while the caption row at the foot sits
    on the darkest ground.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="alp-hero__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="alp-hero__centre">
    {%- if section.settings.show_wordmark -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Decorative — the rail's wordmark link already carries "Bush Riding" as
        the accessible name for the home route, so this stays aria-hidden with
        an empty alt to avoid announcing the wordmark twice.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.wordmark_image != blank -%}
        {{ section.settings.wordmark_image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: class: 'alp-hero__mark', loading: 'eager', alt: '' }}
      {%- else -%}
        <img class="alp-hero__mark" src="{{ 'wordmark-' | append: section.settings.wordmark_tone | append: '.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="" loading="eager" width="1273" height="543">
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.tagline != blank -%}
      <p class="alp-hero__tagline">{{ section.settings.tagline | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The caption row. Naming the country in the frame is the documentary habit
    the brand is built on — and it is also what tells you the page keeps going,
    now that the scroll cue has gone.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.place != blank or section.settings.frame != blank -%}
    <div class="alp-hero__caption">
      <p class="alp-hero__place">{{ section.settings.place | escape }}</p>
      <p class="alp-hero__place">{{ section.settings.frame | escape }}</p>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  The next ride sits directly under the hero on a phone, above the story — the
  one thing a returning rider is most likely to have come for. On desktop the
  rail already carries it down the side of every page, so this is mobile-only;
  showing both on a wide screen would just say it twice.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if section.settings.show_next_ride -%}
  {%- render 'alp-next-ride', variant: 'card', note: section.settings.next_ride_note -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Bush Riding hero",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "Background clip URL",
      "info": "A direct mp4/mov file URL. Takes priority over the image, which becomes its poster."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Hero image",
      "info": "Used on its own when there is no clip, and as the clip's poster when there is."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "poster",
      "label": "Separate poster image",
      "info": "Only needed when the clip should show a different still to the hero image."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Over the photograph"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tagline",
      "label": "Tagline",
      "default": "Made for the detour",
      "info": "Sits under the wordmark, letterspaced."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "place",
      "label": "Caption — place",
      "default": "Mount Beerwah, Glass House Mountains",
      "info": "Bottom left. Naming the country in the frame."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "frame",
      "label": "Caption — frame number",
      "default": "01",
      "info": "Bottom right."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Next ride (mobile only)"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_next_ride",
      "label": "Show the next ride under the hero",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Phones only — the rail carries it on desktop. Pulled live from the Bush Map events feed, and hidden entirely when there is no upcoming ride."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "next_ride_note",
      "label": "Next ride — side note",
      "default": "Free · all welcome"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Wordmark"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_wordmark",
      "label": "Show the wordmark over the photo",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "wordmark_tone",
      "label": "Wordmark tone",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bone", "label": "Bone (default over photography)" },
        { "value": "olive", "label": "Olive" },
        { "value": "sage", "label": "Sage" },
        { "value": "khaki", "label": "Khaki" },
        { "value": "mist", "label": "Mist" },
        { "value": "flare", "label": "Flare" },
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "black", "label": "Black" }
      ],
      "default": "bone"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "wordmark_image",
      "label": "Wordmark image override",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the shipped wordmark artwork above."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Bush Riding hero" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
